|************************************************************************
| DATASHEET-DERIVED IBIS — NOT A VENDOR FILE. FTDI publishes no IBIS
| or SPICE for the FT232R; every table below traces to the published
| points of the FTDI FT232R datasheet (DS_FT232R v1.04), UART/CBUS
| I/O at VCCIO = 5.0 V, STANDARD drive level (the chip default):
|
|   * Table 7 (VCCIO = 5.0 V, standard drive):
|       VOL 0.4 V typ / 0.6 max / 0.3 min at I_sink   = 2 mA
|         -> pulldown slope 200 / 300 / 150 ohm (typ/min/max corners)
|       VOH 4.1 V typ / 3.2 min / 4.9 max at I_source = 2 mA
|         -> pullup drop 0.9 / 1.8 / 0.1 V at 2 mA
|            (450 / 900 / 50 ohm — the P-side spread is the
|            datasheet's own; the min corner IS the guaranteed device)
|   * Table 5: absolute max output current 24 mA (a RATING, not a
|     curve). FTDI publishes NO output curve, so beyond the 2 mA
|     rated point each table continues its measured slope to ~2x
|     rated current and then holds — STATED ASSUMPTION, conservative
|     for SI (a weaker plateau under-predicts drive, never over).
|   * [Ramp]: no transition time is published. Derived as an RC
|     estimate from the measured mid-swing slope into the standard
|     50 pF test load: tau ~ 300 ohm x 50 pF = 15 ns; 20-80% ~ 1.4
|     tau ~ 21 ns -> 3.0 V / 21 ns. STATED ASSUMPTION (physically a
|     lower bound on edge time — again conservative for SI).
|   * C_comp 5 pF: not published; typical CMOS pad class. STATED
|     ASSUMPTION.
|   * Inputs carry an internal 200 kohm pull-up to VCCIO (datasheet
|     footnote to Tables 7-12) — IBIS cannot express it; the entity
|     carries it as input_pullup_k for ERC/DC honesty.
|   * Clamp tables = standard CMOS protection-diode curve.
|
| The HIGH drive level (EEPROM option, Table 10: same voltage limits
| at 6 mA) is deliberately NOT modeled — the chip default is standard
| drive; add an FT_IO_HI model from Table 10 when a board needs it.
|************************************************************************
[IBIS Ver]   4.2
